  "id": "communication-disorder",
  "term": "communication disorder",
  "definition": "Communication disorder is a broad diagnostic category that includes conditions marked by a primary difficulty in communication abilities, especially pragmatic or social use of language. In the provided source, this category includes language disorders, speech sound disorders, childhood-onset fluency disorder (stuttering), and social (pragmatic) communication disorder, but not autism spectrum disorder.",
